+### Listing notes
+
+`GET /notes` always returns a response envelope with `data`, `page`, `pageSize`,
+`total`, and `totalPages`. The optional query parameters are:
+
+- `tag` — exact, case-insensitive tag match.
+- `q` — case-insensitive substring match in the title or body.
+- `page` — 1-indexed positive page number; defaults to `1`.
+- `pageSize` — positive page size from `1` to `100`; defaults to `20`.
+
+`tag` and `q` are trimmed, and empty values are ignored. Filters can be
+combined, and malformed or repeated query parameters return `400`.
